From d3e688e5435e26757f94cecabfc5be2acb57285b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:51:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] nouveau: make R8G8B8A8_UNORM a display target

U_IB carries neither PIPE_BIND_SCANOUT nor PIPE_BIND_DISPLAY_TARGET, so
R8G8B8A8_UNORM could not be a display target and Mesa exposed no RGBA
EGLConfig. droid_add_configs_for_visuals() then leaves only BGRA, and
because AOSP libEGL writes RGBA_8888 onto the window from the chosen
config's channel sizes, every window surface logs

    Native format mismatch: 0x1 != 0x5

even for a client that correctly matches EGL_NATIVE_VISUAL_ID. U_ID is
U_IB plus exactly SCANOUT|DISPLAY_TARGET.

nvc0_formats.c is '#define NOUVEAU_DRIVER 0xc0' plus an #include of this
file and the entry sits outside every #if NOUVEAU_DRIVER block, so this
reaches Ampere as well as Tesla.

Caveat: on a machine where nouveau itself SCANS OUT this may swap red and
blue. It is safe under PRIME render offload -- nouveau renders, the iGPU
scans out -- which is how this port uses NVIDIA.

Change-Id: Ie9ae5d2b2c06d9c131dcbf5eaaa092ee2eb1e230
---
 .../drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_formats.c       | 21 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_formats.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_formats.c
index 4c0934dd06a..7fd468c1bb7 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_formats.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_formats.c
@@ -127,7 +127,26 @@ const struct nv50_format nv50_format_table[PIPE_FORMAT_COUNT] =
    F3(A, B8G8R8X8_UNORM, BGRX8_UNORM, B, G, R, xx, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TD),
    C4(A, B8G8R8A8_SRGB, BGRA8_SRGB, B, G, R, A, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TD),
    F3(A, B8G8R8X8_SRGB, BGRX8_SRGB, B, G, R, xx, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TD),
-   C4(A, R8G8B8A8_UNORM, RGBA8_UNORM, R, G, B, A, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, IB),
+   /* ID, not IB: R8G8B8A8 must be a DISPLAY_TARGET or Mesa creates no RGBA
+    * EGLConfig at all, and every Android window is HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBA_8888.
+    *
+    * droid_add_configs_for_visuals() only exposes BGRA configs when no RGBA one
+    * exists (platform_android.c:823), so the absence here is what makes
+    * SurfaceFlinger pick a BGRA config for an RGBA window:
+    *
+    *     W EGL-MAIN: Native format mismatch: 0x1 != 0x5      x289 in one boot
+    *
+    * The hardware surface format is A8B8G8R8 for both this and B8G8R8A8 above --
+    * the rows differ only in the sampler swizzle -- so nothing new is being
+    * claimed of the display engine that BGRA did not already claim.
+    *
+    * Caveat for anyone reverting this: on a machine where nouveau ITSELF scans
+    * out, the display engine reads the surface format and not the swizzle, so
+    * this may show as swapped red and blue. It is safe under PRIME render
+    * offload, which is how this port uses NVIDIA -- nouveau renders, the iGPU
+    * scans out -- and that is the configuration it was fixed for.
+    */
+   C4(A, R8G8B8A8_UNORM, RGBA8_UNORM, R, G, B, A, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, ID),
    F3(A, R8G8B8X8_UNORM, RGBX8_UNORM, R, G, B, xx, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TB),
    C4(A, R8G8B8A8_SRGB, RGBA8_SRGB, R, G, B, A, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TB),
    F3(A, R8G8B8X8_SRGB, RGBX8_SRGB, R, G, B, xx, UNORM, A8B8G8R8, TB),
